# homekit: the Apple Home bridge, plus the two devices that publish only for it
# (merged into /etc/mosquitto/acl by install.sh, alongside sensors.acl, water.acl and heatronic.acl)

# floor-heating-controller and gate-controller keep no history worth ingesting; they publish the
# retained state document and nothing else.
user floor-heating-controller
topic write floorheating/+/state
topic readwrite floorheating/+/status

user gate-controller
topic write gate/+/state
topic readwrite gate/+/status

# The bridge reads every namespace and writes one topic: the Apple Home thermostat's request (set point,
# pause), which heatronic-controller validates and clamps like any panel's. A leaked bridge password can
# ask for a set point and nothing else: it cannot forge a valve event or a sensor reading.
user homebridge
topic read sensors/#
topic read water/#
topic read floorheating/#
topic read gate/#
topic read heatronic/#
topic write heatronic/room/setpoint/set
